34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows our allocation is down a quarter. Off-site contacts earn nothing, while on-site sessions bill standard rates.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, but only while it ran. The shared nursing round lost a third of visits. We need sustainable models, not temporary fixes.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that visit loss is worrying. My staffing data shows nine unfilled nursing posts and rising agency costs. The midwifery rota has slack, though.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that staffing gap is real. My booking data shows outpatient rooms are full by mid-morning. The car park is jammed before eleven. We have no physical slack.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, those vacancies are a heavy burden. I found the joint clinic closed in a year because neither side held the budget. I worry about similar fragility here.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that fragility is exactly what I fear. With the allocation cut, we cannot afford a program that bleeds money in year two.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, fragility is the norm. The call-back trial proved that. I need to know if any program has a mechanism to sustain itself without constant budget injections.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree. The midwifery slack is a rare opening. A program there would use existing staff, avoiding the agency costs that are straining the wards.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that midwifery slack is a lifeline. But the shuttle only covers four villages. If patients can't get here, the program fails before it starts.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the shuttle gap is real. My data shows outside agreements took fourteen months to sign. We must avoid relying on partners who are slow to commit.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, sustainability is key. I need to know which candidates generate on-site revenue to offset the reduced allocation.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, revenue is a symptom, not a cure. I want to know which candidate has a built-in mechanism to keep patients engaged after the initial funding dries up.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree. But a program that relies on the strained nursing team will just add to the vacancies. We need to use the midwifery slack to keep the roster stable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, I agree. But if the car park is full, no mechanism matters. I need a program that fits the existing physical flow without adding new traffic.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. The joint clinic failed because no one owned the rota. We need a program with a single, clear departmental home to prevent that quiet collapse.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I will focus on candidates that bill on-site. Off-site work earns nothing, so we must prioritize revenue-generating sessions to cover the running costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I will prioritize candidates with a clear, single departmental owner. The call-back trial failed because it lacked that anchor. We need a program that survives without constant oversight.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I will prioritize candidates using the midwifery slack. It avoids the agency costs straining our wards and keeps the roster stable for everyone.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I will prioritize candidates that fit the existing physical flow. No new traffic, no extra parking. The infrastructure must absorb the program without seizing up.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I will prioritize candidates with a single, clear departmental home. The joint clinic failed because ownership was shared. We need one team to truly own the rota and the budget.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
